Usage:

```tsx
// example usage
<CheckoutScreen
  items={cartItems}
  currency="USD"
  deliveryFee={4.99}
  onBack={() => navigate('/cart')}
  onPay={async (address, items) => {
    await api.pay({ address, items });
  }}
/>
```

Notes on the Telegram-specific choices:
- Back navigation and the Pay action are wired to `BackButton`/`MainButton`, not page-drawn controls — per Telegram's rule, duplicating them in-page would collide with the host. "Edit cart" is a secondary in-page link that also routes to `onBack`.
- `fallback-bar` only renders when `window.Telegram.WebApp` is absent, so the screen still works in a plain browser during development.
- Colors read `--tg-theme-*` with light-mode fallbacks, and `useThemeParamsAsCssVars` re-applies them on `themeChanged` so a live dark-mode switch is respected.
- Closing confirmation turns on only while the address form has unsaved input, so a swipe-down won't silently discard it.
